content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-101, AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-22120, filtered-water line (sodium hypochlorite dosed)",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration 3.0 mm/s against Figure 3 of the HF-300 manual: it is above the Zone A/B boundary of 2.8 mm/s and below the Zone B/C boundary of 4.5 mm/s. It sits in Zone B ('Long-term operation'). This is acceptable for continued running and well below Zone D (7.1 mm/s, 'Damage likely - stop the pump'). The site rule to stop immediately applies only in the manufacturer's highest severity zone, so it does not apply.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The manual says to classify the highest vibration reading taken on both bearing housings, with readings in mm/s RMS. The report gives one value of 3.0 mm/s without saying which housing or whether it is RMS. The Zone B classification is therefore valid only if 3.0 mm/s is the highest RMS reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Housing temperature 69 C against the HF-300 bearing housing limits (normal up to 70 C, alarm 80 C, trip 90 C): it is within the normal band but only 1 C below the normal limit. It is 11 C below the alarm limit, so the site priority-1 trigger (above the manufacturer's alarm limit) does not apply. The temperature is measured on the housing surface, consistent with the manual's method.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Dry running for about 15 minutes breaches the manufacturer's requirement. The seal flush is Plan 11 from pump discharge, so the seal had no flush while the pump was dry, and the manual says the pump must never run dry. 'Seal run dry' is a listed cause of shaft seal leakage. No leakage is reported yet, but seal face damage cannot be ruled out.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Most likely risk: the mechanical seal faces were damaged by about 15 minutes of dry running with no Plan 11 flush. This may show up later as leakage at the shaft seal. The corrective action is to replace the mechanical seal (5.2) and check alignment (5.4).",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Possible contributing condition: the housing temperature (69 C) is close to the 70 C normal limit and vibration is in Zone B rather than Zone A. Listed causes for rising bearing temperature and vibration include bearing wear, misalignment, over-greasing, impeller damage and cavitation. Cavitation or NPSH problems are plausible around a tank changeover, but the evidence does not confirm any of these.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "1. Keep P-101 in service; no stop is required now. Immediately take vibration readings (mm/s RMS) on BOTH bearing housings and classify the highest using Figure 3. Stop the pump and notify the reliability engineer if any reading reaches Zone D (above 7.1 mm/s). Plan maintenance if any reading reaches Zone C (above 4.5 mm/s).",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "2. Monitor housing temperature against the limits. If it exceeds 80 C (alarm), raise a P1 work order within the shift. The trip limit is 90 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "3. Inspect the shaft seal for leakage at regular intervals. If leakage appears, carry out mechanical seal replacement per manual 5.2, using the service bulletin parts and torques for this serial (steps 4-12). Also check the reasons for any temperature rise: grease quantity, bearing condition (replace both bearings as a pair per 5.3 if worn) and alignment.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "4. Preparation (planned seal replacement): obtain cartridge seal HF3-450B, NOT HF3-450. Arrange a lifting plan and certified lifting equipment for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly. Obtain a line-break permit.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "5. Electrically isolate and apply LOTO at the MCC. Close the suction and discharge valves, then drain and vent the pump (manual 5.2 step 1).",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "6. Remove the back pull-out assembly (68 kg) using the approved lifting plan. Remove the impeller nut and impeller.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "7. Withdraw the seal and sleeve. Inspect shaft sleeve HF3-455 for scoring and replace it if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. HF3-450B is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement for seal setting is needed.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "8. Fit the new cartridge seal HF3-450B and a new casing gasket. Tighten the seal gland nuts (M10) to 30 Nm per SB-2026-014, not the 25 Nm in Table 5.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "9. Refit the impeller and tighten the impeller nut (M24) to 160 Nm. Refit the back pull-out assembly and tighten the casing bolts (M16) to 210 Nm. If the bearing housing was disturbed, tighten the bearing housing bolts (M12) to 85 Nm. All torques are for lightly oiled threads.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "10. If the work moved the motor or the bearing housing, laser-align the shaft to a parallel offset of 0.05 mm or less and an angular misalignment of 0.05 mm per 100 mm or less.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "11. Remove isolations under permit and confirm the pump is fully primed and vented before start. Never run dry: Plan 11 flush depends on discharge pressure.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "12. After restart, record vibration on both bearing housings and the housing temperature. Confirm vibration is in Zone A/B (4.5 mm/s or less) and temperature is 70 C or less, with no seal leakage.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal, pre-set. Supersedes HF3-450 for serial HF3-22000 and above. Required if seal replacement is carried out.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve. Fit only if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "NOT SPECIFIED IN EVIDENCE",
      "description": "Casing gasket, new, required by manual 5.2 step 5. Part number not given.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For any work inside the pump or on its seal: electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC; mechanical isolation of the suction and discharge valves; line-break permit, with the pump drained and vented first.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, which is over 25 kg. This requires a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "P-101 is on a sodium hypochlorite dosed line. Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves.",
      "citations": [
        "C16",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If vibration reaches the manufacturer's highest zone (Zone D, above 7.1 mm/s RMS), stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If bearing housing temperature exceeds 80 C (manufacturer alarm), raise a P1 work order within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not run the pump dry. Confirm it is primed before any restart, because the seal flush is Plan 11 from discharge.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement: 4.0 hours, 2 technicians (if carried out).",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 hours, 1 technician (only if the motor or bearing housing is moved).",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement (pair): 6.0 hours, 2 technicians. Only needed if the bearings are found worn, noisy or hot.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part: manual 5.2 implies the original component seal HF3-450, while SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) says do NOT fit HF3-450 on HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above; use HF3-450B. P-101 is serial HF3-22120, which is at or above HF3-22000, so the bulletin applies and HF3-450B must be used.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal gland nut torque: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm, while SB-2026-014 gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B. Because serial HF3-22120 falls within the bulletin range, use 30 Nm. Table 5 still applies to the other fasteners (casing bolts 210 Nm, impeller nut 160 Nm, bearing housing bolts 85 Nm), which the bulletin does not change.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve inspection: manual 5.2 says only 'inspect the sleeve for scoring'. The bulletin adds a quantified criterion (replace HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth) and says no sleeve measurement is needed for setting the pre-set HF3-450B. The bulletin criterion applies to this serial.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Is 3.0 mm/s the highest reading of the two bearing housings, and is it an RMS velocity value? The manual requires classifying the highest RMS reading.",
    "Which bearing housing does the 69 C reading come from, and what is the normal baseline or trend? At 1 C below the 70 C normal limit, a rising trend after the dry run would be significant.",
    "Should the seal be replaced proactively after the dry run, or only once leakage appears? The evidence ties seal replacement to the leakage symptom only; reliability engineer decision required.",
    "Seal leak checks and readings after the dry-run event: the evidence does not specify an increased monitoring frequency or duration (only weekly vibration measurement).",
    "Part number for the new casing gasket is not given; the Figure 2 parts list referenced by the exploded view is not in the evidence.",
    "Grease type and quantity for the bearings are not given, so a grease-quantity check cannot be verified against a specification.",
    "Does the evidence cover whether the dry run could have damaged the impeller, wear rings or bearings, or require any inspection of them? It does not, beyond the general troubleshooting table.",
    "Root cause of the dry run during the tank changeover, and whether dry-run or low-flow protection exists on P-101, is not covered by the evidence."
  ]
}
